# Kernl — per-user configuration template.
#
# Copy this file to ~/.config/kernl/.env (the wrapper does it on first run)
# and edit any value you want to override. All keys are optional — the kernel
# has working defaults for everything.
#
# Apply changes:  systemctl --user restart kernl
# Or just stop and re-launch from the desktop launcher.

# ── Dashboard ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HTTP/dashboard port. Change if 3086 collides with another service.
# DASHBOARD_PORT=3086

# ── Security ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Auth token. The HTTP API and /mcp ALWAYS require a Bearer token: leave this
# unset and the kernel generates one on first boot, persisting it (mode 600) as
# data/.kernel-auth-token under the data dir. The launcher prints where to find
# it. Set it here to pin your own instead:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# KERNEL_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Encryption key: encrypts secrets in the SQLite DB (channel passwords,
# OAuth refresh tokens, db-driver credentials). Required for production.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# KERNEL_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ── Graph backend (optional, opt-in via /extensions) ──────────────
# Leave blank for the "Personal" tier — kernel boots with the noop
# graph driver and graph-dependent features degrade gracefully. To
# enable Tier 2, install Neo4j Desktop (or run a container), then go
# to http://localhost:3086/extensions and activate the Neo4j driver.
# These env vars are read by the legacy Neo4jClient as a convenience
# fallback when the user hasn't configured the driver from the UI.
# NEO4J_URI=bolt://localhost:7687
# NEO4J_USER=neo4j
# NEO4J_PASSWORD=

# ── LLM providers (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Configure these *or* set them up via /extensions → "LLM" panel
# (which stores them encrypted in the DB).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=
# LMSTUDIO_BASE_URL=http://localhost:1234/v1

# ── Voice (optional, for STT/TTS features) ────────────────────────
# VOICE_ENABLED=0
# VOICE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# VOICE_ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# ── Disabled modules (optional) ───────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated list of module names to skip at boot. Useful for
# minimal installs:
# DISABLED_MODULES=trading,torrents,cinema
